    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The number of dead is unknown. Later Muslim writers put it between 800,000 and two million, Hulegu claimed two million in a letter to Louis IX, and his count has been called obviously inflated.</li><li>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> flooded the Abbasid army's camp, enclosed the city with a palisade and moat, breached the walls with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siege-engine">siege engines</a> within a few days and refused all terms short of unconditional surrender.</li><li>The fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a> ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid Caliphate</a> there, but modern historians call the claim that it ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islamic-golden-age">Islamic Golden Age</a> simplistic, and large libraries reopened within two years.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>To avoid spilling royal blood, a great taboo for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-mustasim">al-Musta'sim</a> was wrapped in a rolled-up carpet and trampled to death by horses.</p></aside>
    </section>

